  "body": "Process change (#1221, P4, effort:high). Branch synced from `origin/main` at 7a5816cf. The five points of the issue, in order.\n\n## What changed\n\n1. **Refresh only at merge time.** AGENTS.md: new rule \"Refresh only at merge time\" (the maintainer's words quoted, 2026-11-12). A conflicting PR carries `conflicts` and is otherwise left alone. The start-of-session contributor refresh is marked superseded (quote kept). `resolve-conflicts` contributor mode is the merge-time tool; its maintainer `check` asks an author only for a PR in the batch about to merge, and never for others. `review-prs` 2b and `PR-reviewer` follow.\n2. **Planner in the repo.** `cargo xtask merge-plan <PR>...`, `--label <name>`, `--delta <PR> --reviewed <sha>` (plus `--repo`, `--remote`, `--base`). Pure ordering in `xtask/src/merge_plan.rs` (waves, stacks, shared history, the trial callback); pure delta classes in `xtask/src/merge_delta.rs`; git/gh side in `xtask/src/merge_plan_git.rs` (`gh pr list`, `git fetch`, `git merge-tree --write-tree`, `git commit-tree`, `git show --remerge-diff`; nothing checked out, built or pushed). Unit tests in `xtask/src/merge_plan_tests.rs`. One deliberate difference from the reference script: a child whose parent was deferred in wave 1 is deferred too (the reference would have merged it and pulled the parent's changes in silently). Pinned by `three_way_clash_defers_the_merge_and_its_child`.\n3. **A clean merge of main keeps its review.** AGENTS.md section of that name. `--delta` says SAME (only merges of main, empty remerge-diff: review and `merge-ready` stand, no agent) or MECHANICAL (hand edits only in settled files: read by the merging session); DELTA gets a delta review, NEW CODE/Rewritten a full one. The draft rule in AGENTS.md gets the one exception: a clean merge of main keeps the ready flag; any other merge still turns it back into a draft. `review-prs` step 1 skips a head whose new commits are SAME; `PR-reviewer` skip check does the same.\n4. **Only the owner's reviews count** (#1207, \"No, only ours count\"). `review-prs` step 1 query reads markers only from comments/reviews whose author is the owner (`gh repo view NeoTech/Camcraft --json owner`). `merge-ready` without an owner marker for the PR (current head, or an earlier head that `--delta` says SAME/MECHANICAL) is removed with a one-line comment. `PR-reviewer` skip check and `resolve-conflicts check` filter on the author too. AGENTS.md \"Outside PRs are reviewed\" names the rule.\n5. **One gate per batch.** AGENTS.md \"Fixes are tested in the background\": one batch-tier gate per merge batch, not per merge.\n\nAlso: `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 30 to 31. Decision note: `docs/decisions/1221-merge-time-refresh.md`.\n\n**PROCESS_VERSION 31** - what changed: refresh of conflicting PRs only at merge time (no start-of-session refreshes); the merge-order planner (`cargo xtask merge-plan`); clean merges of main keep their review; only the owner's markers and `merge-ready` count.\nWhat a fork must do: stop the start-of-session contributor refreshes; stop marking and labelling your own PRs (the owner's account does that); pull the process files:\n`git checkout upstream/main -- AGENTS.md .claude/agents .claude/skills .claude/PROCESS_VERSION xtask .cargo/config.toml scripts/gate.ps1 scripts/gate.sh scripts/release.ps1 scripts/collect-decisions.ps1 scripts/collect-decisions.sh`\n(the announcement on #681 is made by the merging session when this merges.)\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask --bin xtask merge` : 16 passed, 0 failed. Names: `independent_prs_form_one_wave_docs_first_then_cool_then_hot`, `base_conflict_is_refreshed_after_wave_one_and_is_clean_then`, `pair_clash_on_mechanical_files_is_a_mechanical_refresh`, `code_conflict_after_wave_one_is_by_hand`, `stacked_child_merges_after_its_parent_even_when_it_is_docs_only`, `child_of_a_deferred_parent_is_deferred_too`, `shared_history_puts_the_side_with_fewer_own_commits_first`, `three_way_clash_defers_the_merge_and_its_child`, `render_names_both_waves`, `mechanical_is_the_settled_files_and_snapshots`, and the six `delta_*` tests.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green on the first run (xtask unit tests, 6 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Live, read-only, from the worktree (outputs below): `merge-plan 1211 1216 1203`, `merge-plan --delta 1131 --reviewed 05a44be7`, and `merge-plan --label merge-ready`. The owner lookup and the owner-filtered review query in `review-prs` step 1 were also run live.\n\n```\n$ cargo xtask merge-plan 1211 1216 1203\nbase 7a5816cf\n\nWAVE 1 - merge in this order; no head moves, so no refresh and no delta review (2):\n  #1211  fix(ui): workholding lives under Fixtures in every state\n  #1216  feat(ui): tool kind glyphs on the Tool library catalog rows and the tool picker\n\nWAVE 2 - one at a time: refresh against the main of that moment, check, merge, THEN the next (1):\n  #1203  [by hand] conflicts with main now: crates/ui/src/egui_app/viewcube.rs\n         feat(ui): viewport bottom control bar holds the view buttons (#1198 slice a)\n\n$ cargo xtask merge-plan --delta 1131 --reviewed 05a44be7\nNEW CODE: new commits since the review: a review of `git diff <reviewed>..<head>` for those commits\n  c6091eca merge of main, no hand edits\n  2c1efae9 commit: test(lathe_voice): SinkerBurn is a refused kind on the lathe (#541 wit\n\n$ cargo xtask merge-plan --label merge-ready\nbase 7a5816cf\n\nWAVE 1 - merge in this order; no head moves, so no refresh and no delta review (1):\n  #1216  feat(ui): tool kind glyphs on the Tool library catalog rows and the tool picker\n```\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows only: built and run on Windows here. macOS and Linux are not built in this session (the code uses only `std`, `git` and `gh`; no platform paths).\n- The skills are instructions: the `/resolve-conflicts` and `/review-prs` flows were not run end to end on a real conflicting PR (no PR was refreshed or labelled by this change).\n- Wave 2 with several deferred PRs and a long simulated chain (the commit cache past one or two prefixes) was covered by unit tests with a fake merge oracle, not by a live run.\n- The `--delta` path on a real merge of main with an empty remerge-diff was not run live (no such PR among the three above; the classification is unit-tested).\n\nChangelog: none (build and process only: dev tooling and process text, no product code)\n\nFixes #1221\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
